return array(
	'about_lead' => 'Taira Clinic is a vestibular and balance clinic at 14 Linden Row, Harbourside, Northgate. Dr Lena Ortiz opened it in 2011 so dizziness and unsteadiness could be assessed and retrained in one room.',
	'about_s1_h' => 'Why a balance-only clinic',
	'about_s1_p1' => 'Dr Lena Ortiz opened Taira Clinic in 2011 because dizziness was often handled as a side note. People arrived after being told to rest, then found that rest had not made a tram platform or a shop aisle feel usable again.',
	'about_s1_p2' => 'A clinic that does only vestibular and balance work can keep the tests, the time and the follow-up pointed at that problem. The team looks at how the eyes, the inner ear and the feet work together, then agrees a plan the person can actually practise. We do not treat every medical condition, and we do not claim to.',
	'about_s1_p3' => 'We stay with balance, gaze and the walk back into ordinary streets. If another illness needs a different service, we say so and write to your own doctor.',
	'about_s2_h' => 'The room and the equipment',
	'about_s2_p1' => 'The treatment room is bright and plain: pale walls, light wood, and a foam balance pad on the floor. A gaze chart of dots and arrows hangs on the wall so a clinician can watch how the eyes track without asking you to read letters. Video goggles are used for the gaze test.',
	'about_s2_p2' => 'A balance platform records how weight shifts under the feet. The corridor is long enough for a walking and turning test, with a handrail if you need to pause. Reception has a pale wood bench, and Sofia Marchetti meets you there before you go through. Nothing in the room is for show.',
	'about_s2_p3' => 'Each piece is used in the 60-minute first assessment or in a later session. Seven clinicians work from this one address.',
	'about_s3_h' => 'A typical day',
	'about_s3_p1' => 'On weekdays the desk opens at 08:00. Sofia Marchetti confirms who is due for a 60-minute first assessment and keeps the phone, +1 (555) 014-2200, clear for new bookings. Priya Nair runs gaze and positional testing in the morning.',
	'about_s3_p2' => 'Tomas Weller, Amara Osei and Jonah Lindqvist take rehabilitation sessions through the day, 45 minutes each, and write a short note before the next person. Dr Lena Ortiz sees anyone whose history needs a physician\'s read before a plan is agreed. Daniel Achebe manages the clinic around that list.',
	'about_s3_p3' => 'Saturday runs 08:30 to 13:00 and is used for visits that will not fit a weekday. Sunday and public holidays are closed. Before the door shuts, letters for people\'s own doctors are drafted and the next home exercises are written down.',
