	'assessment_lead' => 'The first assessment is 60 minutes at Taira Clinic. It is how we measure gaze, position and balance before anyone agrees a plan with you.',
	'assessment_s1_h' => 'Sixty minutes and four tests',
	'assessment_s1_p1' => 'The first assessment costs €145 and includes the gaze, positional and balance-platform tests. Priya Nair leads the gaze and positional work. In the video gaze test you wear goggles and follow a target so we can see how your eyes hold and move. There is no reading on the goggles and no letters on the chart.',
	'assessment_s1_p2' => 'The positional test moves you into the positions that set spinning off, including rolling and lying back, which is how BPPV is checked. On the balance platform you stand in socks while the plate records your sway.',
	'assessment_s1_p3' => 'The walking and turning test is done in the corridor: you walk while turning your head, with a clinician beside you and a handrail if you need it. Together the four tests stop us treating every dizzy person with the same exercise.',
	'assessment_s2_h' => 'What should I wear?',
	'assessment_s2_p1' => 'Wear clothes you can move in, because the positional test and the corridor walk ask you to lie back, stand and turn. Wear socks. The balance platform is done in socks, not in outdoor shoes and not barefoot. Bring glasses if you use them for walking. If a doctor has already referred you, say so on the form.',
	'assessment_s2_p2' => 'If you have your own doctor, bring their name, because the last step of the path is a letter back to them. You do not need to arrive with a finished diagnosis. Tell us the main symptom in ordinary words: spinning, unsteady, dizzy after a head injury, falls, visual vertigo, or not sure.',
	'assessment_s2_p3' => 'Also say whether it has lasted under a month, from 1 to 6 months, or more than 6 months.',
	'assessment_s3_h' => 'What you leave with',
	'assessment_s3_p1' => 'At the end of the hour we agree a plan with you, or we tell you that a plan here is not the right next step. A typical plan is 6 sessions over 8–12 weeks plus daily home exercises. Some people need a repositioning visit instead of a long block. Some need the falls-risk screen.',
	'assessment_s3_p2' => 'First appointments are usually within 5 working days of your call or message. Book online or phone +1 (555) 014-2200. The desk email is desk@taira-clinic.example. Use the subject line First assessment request. The clinic is at 14 Linden Row, Harbourside, Northgate. We do not promise a result from the tests.',
	'assessment_s3_p3' => 'We promise the hour, the four measures, and a plan you have heard in plain language before you leave.',
