	'mt1_t' => 'Measure',
	'mt1_x' => 'The first assessment takes 60 minutes. You sit in video goggles while Priya Nair records your gaze, then we test position on the couch and stance on the balance platform. The three tests say whether this is a crystal, a nerve, a migraine pattern, a concussion effect or a mix. You leave knowing which one we are treating.',
	'mt2_t' => 'Retrain',
	'mt2_x' => 'Sessions are 45 minutes on the foam pad and in the corridor. Eyes closed, arms crossed, head turns while you walk: the drill matches the failed signal, with a clinician spotting. A repositioning visit for BPPV is shorter, 30 minutes, when the tests say that is the job. Two short exercises a day sit between the visits.',
	'mt3_t' => 'Return',
	'mt3_x' => 'The last part is the place that set you off: the kerb, the market, the quiet road, the aisle with a list. We grade it. A review closes the block, and we write to your own doctor so the plan does not stay inside this building. A typical plan is six sessions over eight to twelve weeks. Outcomes differ from person to person.',
	'mt_h' => 'Measure, retrain, return',
